  "originalQuery": "You are managing a multi-regional application that utilizes Google Cloud Spanner for its database needs. The application requires both read and write operations to be as low latency as possible for users in Europe and Asia. Which configuration should you choose to meet these requirements?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Create two separate Spanner instances, one in Europe and one in Asia, and synchronize them using Cloud Dataflow.<br/>B. Use a global HTTP(S) load balancer to direct traffic to the nearest Spanner instance based on the user's location.<br/>C. Deploy a single-region Spanner instance in Europe and route all Asian traffic to this instance.<br/>D. Set up a multi-regional Spanner instance configured for both Europe and Asia regions.",
